    "body": "## Overview\n\nBatch per-expert token count GPU synchronization into a single CPU transfer in MoE eager-mode paths, eliminating N sequential `.item()` GPU syncs per forward pass.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Eliminates per-expert `.item()` GPU synchronization in `fused_batched_moe.py` eager path\n- Eliminates per-expert `.item()` GPU synchronization in `batched_deep_gemm_moe.py` UE8M0 scale packing loop\n- Reduces 64+ sequential GPU syncs to 1 GPU-to-CPU transfer for 64-expert models\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`: all passed\n- Code path: the `_is_capturing_or_compiling()` guard ensures CUDA graph / inductor paths are unaffected (they use `hidden_states.shape[1]` directly, no GPU sync)\n- The `.tolist()` call produces a Python list of ints, equivalent to `int(tensor[i].item())` for each element but in a single transfer\n\n## Details\n\nThe eager-mode MoE expert loop called `.item()` on the GPU tensor `expert_num_tokens` once per expert, forcing a GPU synchronization each time. With 64+ experts this adds 64+ sequential GPU syncs per forward pass.\n\nReplace with a single `.tolist()` call before the loop, then index the CPU list. Each `.tolist()` is one GPU-to-CPU transfer; each `.item()` is a separate synchronization point.\n\nApply the same fix to the UE8M0 scale packing loop in `batched_deep_gemm_moe.py`, where `tokens_per_expert[e_idx].item()` was called per expert.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
